# Auto push completed work to `main`

When a coding task is **finished** (bugfix, feature, or polish the user asked for):

1. **Commit** the relevant project files to `main` (do not wait for the user to ask again).
2. **Push** to `origin main` immediately after a successful commit.
3. Tell the user the commit hash / short summary and that it was pushed.

## Include
- Source code, docs, configs related to the completed work

## Exclude
- Secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens, `google.drive.token.json`, service-account JSON)
- Large/local media unless the user explicitly asked to commit them (`uploads/avatars/*`, new hero banner binaries)
- Scratch / temp (`.superpowers/`, one-off `scripts/check-*.js` unless part of the deliverable)

## Commit style
- Concise message focusing on why (feat/fix/style/docs)
- PowerShell-safe commit message (plain `-m "..."` is fine on Windows)

## Exceptions
- If push fails (auth/network/conflicts), report the error and stop — do not force-push.
- Never `push --force` to `main`.
- If the user says not to push for a specific task, skip for that task only.
